Bugs found while verifying
--------------------------
1. `services/db.connect` opened SQLite with the default `check_same_thread=True`.
   FastAPI runs a sync generator dependency and its sync endpoint on *different*
   threadpool threads, so the nine concurrent card fetches 500'd. Now
   `check_same_thread=False` — safe, since every request opens and closes its own
   connection.
2. `market_data.batch_refresh` stamped every quote `date.today()`, including a
   stale NAV and a cached read. yfinance 404s on every AMFI code, so once any
   history existed the NAV feed was never consulted and the cached price was
   re-stamped as today — the two newest rows per symbol held the same number and
   the day change read a false 0.00.
3. `night_worker.weekly_gap_only_refresh` did not fetch anything: it carried the
   last price forward one row per calendar day. Same effect, nightly. It now
   inserts the feed's real points past `MAX(date)`.
   (20 fabricated rows written during this session's own verification runs were
   deleted; the DB holds published quotes only.)

